WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:19.628
Mary walked down the path that led to the gate in the shrubbery.

2
00:00:19.629 --> 00:00:24.297
When she passed through the gate, she found herself in a big garden.

3
00:00:24.298 --> 00:00:27.223
There was a pool with an old fountain.

4
00:00:27.224 --> 00:00:32.917
But the fountain was turned off, and the garden's flower beds were bare and wintry.

5
00:00:32.918 --> 00:00:38.349
Mary saw that the path came to an end at a brick wall.

6
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.157
A green door in the wall stood open.

7
00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:46.940
She went through the door and came upon a new garden with walls all around it.

8
00:00:46.941 --> 00:00:50.442
She spied another open green door.

9
00:00:50.443 --> 00:00:55.505
Through that one she could see cold frames covering some of the garden beds.

10
00:00:55.506 --> 00:01:00.286
She seemed to be in the midst of a series of walled gardens.

11
00:01:00.287 --> 00:01:04.553
"This place is so bare and ugly," thought Mary.

12
00:01:04.554 --> 00:01:11.097
"It might be nicer in summer when things are green, but there is nothing pretty about it now."

13
00:01:11.098 --> 00:01:14.663
Soon an old gardener came through the door.

14
00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:20.647
He did not seem pleased to see her, but then again she was not pleased with his garden.

15
00:01:20.648 --> 00:01:24.026
"What is this place?" Mary asked.

16
00:01:24.027 --> 00:01:28.160
"One of the kitchen gardens, where we grow fruits and vegetables."

17
00:01:28.161 --> 00:01:30.211
"Can I walk through it?"

18
00:01:30.212 --> 00:01:35.411
"If you like, but there's nothing to see."

19
00:01:35.412 --> 00:01:41.238
Mary went through the second green door and saw that the cold frames were covering vegetables.

20
00:01:41.239 --> 00:01:46.118
In this garden was another green door, but it was closed.

21
00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:51.930
"I hope this is the secret garden," said Mary as she tried the handle.

22
00:01:51.931 --> 00:01:56.876
But she opened the door quite easily and found herself in an orchard.

23
00:01:56.877 --> 00:02:03.015
It, too, was surrounded by a wall. Mary didn't see any more doors.

24
00:02:03.016 --> 00:02:09.471
She noticed the wall seemed to extend beyond the orchard, and she could see trees growing above the wall.

25
00:02:09.472 --> 00:02:15.151
A bird with a bright red breast was sitting on the topmost branch of one tree.

26
00:02:15.152 --> 00:02:22.417
Suddenly he burst into song. It was as if he were calling to her.

27
00:02:22.418 --> 00:02:28.631
She stopped and listened, and somehow his cheerful, friendly song gave her a pleasant feeling.

28
00:02:28.632 --> 00:02:32.218
Even a disagreeable little girl may be lonely.

29
00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:38.098
The big, closed house and big, bare moor had made Mary feel all alone in the world.

30
00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:43.891
But now the bird brought a look onto her sour face that was almost a smile.

31
00:02:43.892 --> 00:02:48.045
She watched him until he flew off the branch.

32
00:02:48.046 --> 00:02:52.291
"I believe that tree is in the secret garden," she said.

33
00:02:52.292 --> 00:02:58.480
She walked back to the first kitchen garden and found the old man digging there.

34
00:02:58.481 --> 00:03:01.400
"I went into the orchard," said Mary.

35
00:03:01.401 --> 00:03:04.632
"There was no door into the next garden."

36
00:03:04.633 --> 00:03:08.613
"What garden?" the old man said sharply.

37
00:03:08.614 --> 00:03:11.339
"The one on the other side of the wall.

38
00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.208
A bird with a red breast was sitting in one of the trees."

39
00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:20.906
A slow smile spread over the old man's face. "That's the robin."

40
00:03:20.907 --> 00:03:25.505
He turned toward the orchard and whistled softly.

41
00:03:25.506 --> 00:03:29.033
The next moment a wonderful thing happened.

42
00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:33.647
The bird flew toward them and landed near the gardener's foot.

43
00:03:33.648 --> 00:03:38.493
"Will he always come when you call him?" Mary asked in a whisper.

44
00:03:38.494 --> 00:03:42.328
"Yes. I've known him since he first tried to fly.

45
00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:45.901
When he flew over the wall, he was too weak to fly back.

46
00:03:45.902 --> 00:03:48.616
We got to be friends.

47
00:03:48.617 --> 00:03:54.073
Then when he finally flew back, he found the rest of his brood had left the nest.

48
00:03:54.074 --> 00:03:57.510
He was lonely, so he returned to me."

49
00:03:57.511 --> 00:04:02.199
Mary took a step closer to the robin. "I'm lonely."

50
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:08.914
"I'm lonely too except when he's with me." The old man began to dig again.

51
00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.633
"He's the only friend I've got."

52
00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:14.985
"What's your name?" asked Mary.

53
00:04:14.986 --> 00:04:18.849
"Ben Weatherstaff. You and I are a bit alike.

54
00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:23.172
We're not good-looking, and we're both as sour as we look."

55
00:04:23.173 --> 00:04:27.024
Mary was surprised at the bold way Ben spoke to her.

56
00:04:27.025 --> 00:04:30.469
She wondered if what he said was true.

57
00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:34.981
Suddenly there was a clear rippling sound, and she turned around.

58
00:04:34.982 --> 00:04:40.186
The robin had flown into an apple tree and seemed to be singing right to her.

59
00:04:40.187 --> 00:04:44.260
"He's made up his mind to be friends with you," said Ben.

60
00:04:44.261 --> 00:04:49.419
"Would you make friends with me?" Mary asked the robin in a kind voice.

61
00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:55.016
The robin didn't answer. Instead he flew away.

62
00:04:55.017 --> 00:04:59.468
"He has flown into the garden with no door," said Mary.

63
00:04:59.469 --> 00:05:05.037
"He lives there. He's probably courting some lady robin who lives among the roses."

64
00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.477
"There are roses in that garden?"

65
00:05:07.478 --> 00:05:12.549
Ben began to dig again. "There were ten years ago," he mumbled.

66
00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:17.691
"I'd like to see them," said Mary. "Do you know of a door?"

67
00:05:17.692 --> 00:05:19.910
"There's none that anyone can find.

68
00:05:19.911 --> 00:05:23.656
Don't go looking for any doors," Ben warned her.

69
00:05:23.657 --> 00:05:27.072
"I must get on with my work now. Go on and play."

70
00:05:27.073 --> 00:05:35.462
And with that he threw his shovel over his shoulder and walked away.
